    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/Talent-Acquisition-Advisor/615-en_GB": {
      "title": "Talent Acquisition Advisor Job Details",
      "description": "Talent Acquisition Advisor Job Details | demontfort Talent Acquisition Advisor We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Job Alerts Link Talent Acquisition Advisor Apply now Requisition Id: 615 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Part-time Employee Weekly Hours: 22.20 Maximum Salary: 38,784.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 32,080.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Talent Acquisition Advisor (0.6 FTE, Pro rata) – Fixed Term Contract until September 2027 De Montfort University (DMU) is looking for a proactive, customer‑focused Talent Acquisition Advisor (part‑time, 0.6 FTE) to support the attraction and recruitment of senior leaders and specialist roles. This is a fantastic opportunity to join a forward‑thinking People Services team and help deliver an outstanding recruitment experience that enables DMU to secure the very best talent in a competitive market. We’re specifically looking for someone with strong end‑to‑end recruitment experience, including proactive sourcing capability across specialist and hard‑to‑fill roles.This role is hybrid, with one day a week onsite at our Leicester campus. Role Reporting to the Talent Acquisition Manager, you will play a key role in delivering a high-quality, end-to-end recruitment service. You will: Partner with hiring managers to develop proactive recruitment plans and manage the full vacancy lifecycle for Academic and Professional hires Provide expert advice and guidance on sourcing, attraction and selection for senior and specialist role s Actively source candidates through methods such as LinkedIn and other channels, building pipelines of talent Work with external agencies to deliver specialist recruitment campaigns Support onsite assessment ensuring an exceptional candidate experience Deliver recruitment training and guidance to managers to support effective hiring decisions Monitor performance against KPIs and contribute to improving service delivery Support continuous improvement of recruitment systems, processes and candidate experience Ideal Candidate We’re looking for someone who is organised, insightful and passionate about recruitment, with: Proven end‑to‑end recruitment experience within an in‑house Talent Acquisition team, including proactive sourcing for specialist and hard‑to‑fill roles. Experience working in a similar Talent Acquisition or recruitment role, ideally within higher education, the public sector, or a professional services environment. Strong knowledge of recruitment processes, sourcing techniques and candidate engagement. Experience supporting a range of stakeholders, including senior leaders. Excellent communication skills and the ability to build strong relationships. We’re excited to hear from candidates who are passionate about delivering an outstanding recruitment experience and committed to making a real impact at DMU. If you care deeply about candidate experience , proactive recruitment and supporting a values‑driven university, we’d be delighted to receive your application. This is a fixed‑term contract until September 2027 . To view the job description and person specification, please click here Contact Please contact Imran Umar directly  on imran.umar@dmu.ac.uk for any questions or an informal discussion about the role. Apply now Information at a Glance Share Copy Link Email LinkedIn X Facebook De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are