    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/Senior-Cloud-&-Infrastructure-Analyst/695-en_GB": {
      "title": "Senior Cloud & Infrastructure Analyst Job Details",
      "description": "Senior Cloud & Infrastructure Analyst Job Details | demontfort Senior Cloud & Infrastructure Analyst We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Job Alerts Link Senior Cloud & Infrastructure Analyst Apply now Requisition Id: 695 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Full-time Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Maximum Salary: 56,535.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 44,746.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Senior Cloud & Infrastructure Analyst Leicester Hybrid – 2 days onsite The Digital and Technology Directorate at De Montfort University (DMU) is central to transforming how the university delivers digital value. We are modernising services through cloud adoption, reducing technical debt and implementing a product operating model that supports agile delivery and operational excellence. Our work spans AI, automation, endpoint management, cyber security and infrastructure modernisation, ensuring resilient, user‑focused and future‑ready digital services across DMU. The Role As a Senior Cloud & Infrastructure Analyst, you will act as a technical subject matter expert across DMU’s hybrid infrastructure. This includes public cloud services primarily Microsoft Azure and on‑premises technologies such as Windows and Linux servers, VMware virtualisation, NetApp storage and a range of hybrid and security platforms. You will lead on designing and implementing hybrid cloud and on‑premises solutions, including assessment and documentation of existing infrastructure landscapes. You will play a key role in DMU’s early‑stage cloud adoption journey, developing infrastructure roadmaps and guiding the transition to scalable, resilient and secure cloud platforms aligned with the university’s digital transformation strategy. The role requires strong analytical capability, the ability to balance operational continuity with transformation, and a deep understanding of hybrid cloud principles, cloud security architectures and modern infrastructure technologies. You will be part of the Platforms and Connectivity team, working closely with IT Security, Architecture and Data colleagues across a diverse portfolio of technology projects. Key Responsibilities Act as a technical SME and administrator for DMU’s hybrid infrastructure. Contribute significantly to the Cloud Adoption Strategy, including managing Azure workloads and assessing new and existing solutions. Design scalable, resilient cloud solutions and lead migration of legacy systems to modern platforms. Optimise hybrid cloud environments for cost, security and performance. Embed security‑by‑design principles and leverage security data to inform decision‑making. Essential: Extensive experience designing and implementing hybrid cloud and on‑premises solutions. Strong experience managing complex IT platforms (Windows/Linux, VMware, NetApp, security). Proficiency in modern infrastructure technologies including virtualisation, containerisation or serverless. Strong understanding of hybrid cloud, cloud security architectures and secure design principles. Ability to communicate effectively with technical and non‑technical audiences. Willingness to provide out‑of‑hours support when required. Degree in a related field or equivalent experience. Desirable: Relevant public cloud certifications, ideally Microsoft Azure (AZ‑900, AZ‑104, AZ‑305). Additional certifications (VMware, NetApp, Microsoft, IT Security). Experience with IaC (Terraform, ARM, Bicep) and DevOps pipelines. Experience in higher education or similarly complex environments. To view the job description and person specification click here Application Closing Date: Sunday 01 November 2026 Please complete your application via the link provided and include a supporting statement outlining how you meet the essential criteria. Contact For further information please contact:- Dean Brockley - Head of Platforms & Connectivity email : dean.brockley@gmail.com Apply now Information at a Glance Share Copy Link Email LinkedIn X Facebook De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required