    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/Porter/668-en_GB": {
      "title": "Porter Job Details",
      "description": "Porter Job Details | demontfort Porter We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Job Alerts Link Porter Apply now Requisition Id: 668 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Part-time Employee Weekly Hours: 20.00 Maximum Salary: 24,533.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 24,533.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities De Montfort University is a university of quality and distinctiveness, distinguished by our life-changing research, dynamic international partnerships, vibrant links with business and our commitment to excellence in learning, teaching and the student experience. We offer more than 300 courses at foundation, undergraduate and postgraduate, many of which offer professional accreditations, and links to industry or work experience. DMU undergraduate and postgraduate courses receive continual input from leading employers and professional bodies and are underpinned by world-leading research. This ensures they remain relevant and up-to-date and provide students with the skills and experience employers expect from candidates in a competitive job market. Role An opportunity has arisen for an enthusiastic and highly motivated individual to join the Campus Services team, working on our city campus to help fulfil our commitment to providing a quality porterage service to support university business. We are seeking a reliable and motivated Porter to join our team. As part of Estates and Facilities, you will help create a positive environment that supports the learning, teaching, and research activities of the University. This is a hands-on role where attention to detail, pride in your work, and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential. You will work as part of a supportive team to provide porterage support the University's buildings, ensuring all spaces are prepared for external events, teaching and exams to name a few, so they remain welcoming for our diverse community and focuses on the student experience As a Porter, this busy and varied role incorporates all duties related to movement of furniture, equipment and materials to support the university business needs. Assistance with ceremonies and corporate events and ensuring all buildings are prepared to the highest standard to enhance our facilities for all students, staff and visitors. Ideal Candidate We are looking for an individual who: Will ideally have previous similar experience. Holds a full UK driving licence. Will have experience of manual handling operations and use of associated equipment. You will be provided with training when you join the team. Takes pride in delivering high standards of workmanship. Has a positive attitude and strong work ethic. Can work independently and as part of a team. Are reliable, punctual, and trustworthy. Demonstrate a commitment to excellent customer service. Can follow safe working procedures, instructions, and health and safety requirements. Has good communication skills. Are willing to undertake training and development as required. Are able to work unsocial hours, including weekends as required. The position is part of a small team on campus, working within allocated university buildings. You will be required to work 20 hours per week, Monday to Sunday between 6:00am-8:00pm, to suit the needs of university business. The salary shown will be pro-rated down to reflect the part time hours however you will also receive an unsociable hours payment, per hour on top of your normal hourly rate for all hours worked before 8:00am, after 8:00pm and at weekends. To view the job description and person specification click here Contact To discuss any details of this role, please contact Scott Batts, Post & Porterage Team Leader on scott.batts@dmu.ac.uk or 0116 2078657 Apply now Information at a Glance Share Copy Link Email LinkedIn X Facebook De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the follow