    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/LecturerSenior-Lecturer-in-Audiology-2-Year-Fixed-Term/602-en_GB": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Audiology",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Audiology - 2 Year Fixed Term Job Details | demontfort We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Audiology - 2 Year Fixed Term Apply now Requisition Id: 602 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Full-time Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Maximum Salary: 56,535.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 39,906.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 28/10/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Faculty / Directorate De Montfort University (DMU) is a vibrant, ambitious and inclusive learning institution. We have been awarded the ‘Collaborative Award for Teaching Excellence’ from Advance HE for the work around Decolonising DMU and are the first university to receive the silver award in the Race Equality Charter (REC). The Faculty of Health and Life Sciences at De Montfort University educates and develops professionals who make a significant difference to people’s lives, health, wellbeing and society. It is home to the Leicester School of Allied Health Sciences in which this post will be based. Role You would work as part of a team, primarily delivering high-quality teaching and training across a range of programmes. In addition to adult aural diagnostics and rehabilitation, we are seeking expertise in anatomy and physiology of the auditory pathway and/or acoustics. You would contribute to teaching and training across our programmes, including the development and delivery of new programmes and short courses. The role will also involve being a key member of the academic placement team, supporting both students on placement and placement providers. The Audiology section of the school is one of the largest in the country and boasts excellent facilities with the latest clinical equipment. It offers an excellent opportunity for engagement in enterprise activities and research. Ideal Candidate The ideal candidate should be experienced and be enthusiastic about the subject. They should possess a broad foundation in audiology and be able to contribute across a range of teaching and training activities. While a postgraduate qualification in Audiology would be advantageous, we are interested to hear from candidates with substantial clinical experience. The candidate must be passionate about teaching and training, demonstrate creativity, and be committed to developing and expanding professional networks. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Apply now Information at a Glance De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Open