. In addition to adult aural diagnostics and rehabilitation, we are seeking candidates with experience and expertise in paediatric audiology, including assessment and rehabilitation. You would contribute to teaching and training across our programmes, including the development and delivery of new programmes and short courses. The Audiology section of the school is one of the largest in the country and boasts excellent facilities with the latest clinical equipment.  It offers an excellent opportunity for engagement in enterprise activities and research. Ideal Candidate The ideal candidate will have relevant experience and a genuine enthusiasm for the subject. They should possess a broad foundation in audiology and be able to contribute across a range of teaching and training activities. While a postgraduate qualification in Audiology would be advantageous, we welcome applications from candidates with substantial clinical experience in paediatric audiology. The successful candidate will be passionate about teaching and training, demonstrate creativity and initiative, and be committed to developing and expanding professional networks. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Contact For More Information, please contact: Rakesh Patel Deputy Head of School of Leicester School of Allied Health Sciences email: rkpatel@dmu.ac.uk Apply now Information at a Glance De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager 