    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/Weekend-Cleaner/663-en_GB": {
      "title": "Weekend Cleaner Job Details",
      "description": "Weekend Cleaner Job Details | demontfort Weekend Cleaner We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Job Alerts Link Weekend Cleaner Apply now Requisition Id: 663 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Part-time/Annualised hours Employee Weekly Hours: 3.33 Maximum Salary: 24,533.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 24,533.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Role An opportunity has arisen for an enthusiastic and highly motivated individual to join the Campus Services team, working on our city campus to help fulfil our commitment to providing a quality cleaning service to the academic environment. We are seeking reliable and motivated Cleaners to join our team. As part of Estates and Facilities, you will help create a positive environment that supports the learning, teaching, and research activities of the University. This is a hands-on role where attention to detail, pride in your work, and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential. You will work as part of a supportive team to maintain the University's buildings to the highest standards, ensuring they remain clean, safe, and welcoming for our diverse community and focuses on the student experience As a weekend Cleaner, this busy and varied role incorporates all duties related to both general and reactive cleaning, assistance with ceremonies and corporate events and ensuring all buildings are maintained to the highest standard to enhance our facilities for all students, staff and visitors. Ideal Candidate We are looking for an individual: Who will ideally have previous cleaning experience You will have experience of using modern cleaning methods and using cleaning machinery and tools. You will be provided with training when you join the team. Take pride in delivering high standards of cleanliness. Have a positive attitude and strong work ethic. Can work independently and as part of a team. Are reliable, punctual, and trustworthy. Demonstrate a commitment to excellent customer service. Can follow cleaning procedures, instructions, and health and safety requirements. Have good communication skills. Are willing to undertake training and development as required. The position is to work as part of a small team on campus at the weekend. You will be required to work 10 hours (Saturday and Sunday 06:00am – 11:00am), on a one weekend in three rota totalling 17.33 weekends per year. The salary shown will be pro-rated down to reflect the part time hours however you will also receive a 50% unsociable hours payment, per hour on top of your normal hourly rate. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Apply now Information at a Glance Share Copy Link Email LinkedIn X Facebook De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As 