    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/Technician-%28Pharmaceutics-&-Optometry%29-Maternity-cover-0_75-FTE/721-en_GB": {
      "title": "Technician (Pharmaceutics & Optometry)",
      "description": "Technician (Pharmaceutics & Optometry) - Maternity cover 0.75 FTE Job Details | demontfort We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Technician (Pharmaceutics & Optometry) - Maternity cover 0.75 FTE Apply now Requisition Id: 721 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Part-time Employee Weekly Hours: 27.75 Maximum Salary: 31,236.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 26,707.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities Please note, this is a 0.75 FTE role for 27.75 hours per week and will be expected to work until 5.30pm. The working pattern can be discussed further wit hthe hiring manager. The post covers for a maternity leave and will last for a fixed term period or when the original post holder returns. MAIN DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Support the effective running of laboratories, clinical spaces and specialist teaching facilities for undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, research and practice. Assist with practical classes, liaise with academic staff, support project and experiment development, and troubleshoot technical issues. Complete tasks assigned by the Technical Team Leader, meeting deadlines and maintaining quality, accuracy and appropriate quality control when preparing materials and chemicals. Demonstrate specialist equipment, instruments, apparatus, techniques and software to staff and students. Carry out routine equipment maintenance and ensure compliance with health and safety requirements. Provide clear guidance and develop standard operating procedures (SOPs) where necessary. Assist with reviewing and updating risk assessments, COSHH documentation and compliance records in line with university policies. Follow safe working procedures and advise staff and students on the safe and correct use of equipment and facilities. Monitor the safe distribution, storage, use and disposal of hazardous materials, chemicals and waste. Support stock control and maintain relevant databases. Keep technical spaces and equipment clean, tidy and safe. Manage consumables, including replenishment, stock control, ordering and associated financial administration, under the Team Leader's direction. Maintain the technical asset register and identify equipment requiring replacement. Provide Goods Inwards support when required. Maintain high technical standards and consistency across technical spaces. Undertake continuing professional development and develop skills to meet the university's changing needs. Support late-finishing classes and assessments when required. Assist with open days and outreach events. Undertake First Aid training to support university first aid and evacuation requirements. Support the Technician Commitment and initiatives promoting technician visibility, recognition, career development and sustainability. Undertake Portable Appliance Testing (PAT) in technical areas and maintain relevant training. Where applicable, design, manufacture and repair components for other university areas when requested. Undertake other duties appropriate to the grade as reasonably required. The role may require a DBS check, with the level determined at offer stage. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Contact For more information about the role please contact: Dr Niran Patel - niran.patel@dmu.ac.uk Skills Problem-Solving Attention to Detail Communication Time Management Flexibility Adaptability Initiative Teamwork Education HND/HNC BSc / BA Degree Apply now Information at a Glance De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie n