    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/Employer-Engagement-Manager/694-en_GB": {
      "title": "Employer Engagement Manager Job Details",
      "description": "Employer Engagement Manager Job Details | demontfort Employer Engagement Manager We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Job Alerts Link Employer Engagement Manager Apply now Requisition Id: 694 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Full-time Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Maximum Salary: 43,482.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 39,906.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Job Description: Main duties, responsibilities and additional context De Montfort University De Montfort University is a university of quality and distinctiveness, distinguished by our life-changing research, dynamic international partnerships, vibrant links with business and our commitment to excellence in learning, teaching and the student experience. The Role The role reports to the Student Employment Manager and leads the Employer Engagement Team. It is responsible for the development and maintenance of effective and beneficial relationships with employers to enhance graduate outcomes for DMU students. The role leads and manages a small but dynamic team in the management of relationships with strategically aligned employer partners plus the identification, approach and development of new relationships with employers which deliver positive outcomes as part of the Employer Engagement strategy. Ideal Candidate You will have experience of leading a high-performing team, ideally in a careers or relationship-management context. We are looking for someone who can bring excellent stakeholder management skills to deliver high-quality employment opportunities to students. The successful candidate will need to be confident communicating with others, well-organised and excellent at balancing priorities. Strong interpersonal skills will be vital, as will solid skills for data analysis and reporting. Interview dates likely to be w/c 16th November. To view the job description and person specification, please click here The Team You will join the Employer Engagement Team in DMU’s award winning Careers Team, which sits within the Directorate of Student Life and Learning Services (SLLS). This directorate is responsible for providing a wide and diverse range of services to all our students including Student Wellbeing, Careers & Employability, Student Finance and Academic Support. For an informal chat about the role please contact daniel.middler@dmu.ac.uk Apply now Information at a Glance Share Copy Link Email LinkedIn X Facebook De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort U