    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/Senior-Lecturer-Occupational-Therapy/703-en_GB": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer Occupational Therapy Job Details",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer Occupational Therapy Job Details | demontfort We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Senior Lecturer Occupational Therapy Apply now Requisition Id: 703 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Full-time Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Maximum Salary: 56,535.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 44,746.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities At De Montfort University, you'll join a Faculty that is passionate about developing professionals who change lives. The Faculty of Health and Life Sciences brings together an ambitious community of educators, practitioners, researchers and students across four specialist schools: Allied Health Sciences, Applied Social Sciences, Nursing and Midwifery, and Pharmacy. Our graduates go on to make a tangible difference to individuals, families and communities, improving health, wellbeing and life opportunities across the region and beyond. This is an especially exciting time to join us, as part of our commitment to being an Empowering University, we are investing significantly in the future of healthcare education, creating world-class learning environments that prepare students for the realities of contemporary practice. Occupational Therapy is a key strategic growth area within the Faculty, and we are seeking a leader who is excited by the opportunity to shape something new, distinctive and impactful. Role We are seeking 2 Academic Leaders, you will provide the strategic, curriculum and professional leadership required to successfully develop and establish the programme within the School of Allied Health Sciences. Working collaboratively with colleagues, students, people with lived experience, employers, independent practitioner and practice partners, you will shape an innovative curriculum that prepares graduates to thrive in a changing health and social care landscape. You will play a central role in building the programme's identity and reputation, ensuring it embodies our commitment to inclusivity, equity and social impact. Through strong external engagement, you will develop partnerships that create outstanding learning opportunities and position De Montfort University as a recognised contributor to occupational therapy education nationally and regionally. Ideal Candidate We are looking for 2 HCPC registered occupational therapist with the vision, energy and leadership skills to create something exceptional. The post holders will be responsible for ensuring regulatory and professional requirements are met, maintaining the highest standards of academic quality and professional education. You will bring: Experience of programme leadership or practice-based learning within higher education in the UK. A passion for developing future healthcare professionals. Experience of inclusive curriculum design and programme development aligned with contemporary occupational therapy practice and workforce needs . An active commitment to widening participation, inclusion and social justice. Experience of driving student recruitment, retention and success to establish a thriving programme community. A collaborative approach and the ability to develop effective partnerships across health, social care and community settings. Enthusiasm for innovation and a desire to shape the future of occupational therapy and Allied Health Professions education. Join Us This is an opportunity to build a programme that reflects the very best of occupational therapy and the values of De Montfort University. You will help create graduates who are empowered to tackle health inequalities, support participation and independence, and deliver person-centred care across diverse communities. To view the JDPS, please click here Contact Development and Support As a postholder you will be expected to work towards HEA Fellowship and a PgCert in Higher Education if not already held. De Montfort University provides support for both. You will have the opportunity to contribute to the wider strategic ambitions of the School, Faculty and University through leadership, scholarship, research, enterprise and external engagement. Join Us You will join a growing School of Allied Health Sciences with a strong commitment to educational innovation, interdisciplinary collaboration and delivering real-world impact. Together, we are developing the next generation of professionals who will transform lives and strengthen communities. If you are excited by the opportunity to create, lead and grow a new Occupational Therapy programme that places social justice, empowerment and community wellbeing at its heart, we would love to hear from you. We particularly welcome applications from racially minoritised and other under-represented groups and are committed to inclusive and culturally responsive practice. For more information about the role please contact Dr Kim Stuart, Head of School Allied Health Sciences via email kim.stuart@dmu.ac.uk Apply now Information at a Glance De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may