es in a competitive job market. Role An opportunity has arisen for an enthusiastic and highly motivated individual to join the Campus Services team, working on our city campus to help fulfil our commitment to providing a quality cleaning service to the academic environment. We are seeking a reliable and motivated External Window Cleaner to join our team. As part of Estates and Facilities, you will help create a positive environment that supports the learning, teaching, and research activities of the University. This is a hands-on role where attention to detail, pride in your work, and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential. You will work as part of a supportive team to maintain the University's buildings to the highest standards, ensuring they remain clean, safe, and welcoming for our diverse community and focuses on the student experience As an External Window Cleaner, this role incorporates all duties related to both external and internal window cleaning, using a trailer-based water fed pole system externally, with more traditional widow cleaning methods internally. Ideal Candidate We are looking for an individual who: Will ideally have previous cleaning experience Will have experience of using modern cleaning methods and using cleaning machinery and tools. You will be provided with training when you join the team. Holds a full driving licence. Takes pride in delivering high standards of cleanliness. Have a positive attitude and strong work ethic. Can work independently and as part of a team. Are reliable, punctual, and trustworthy. Demonstrate a commitment to excellent customer service. Can follow cleaning procedures, instructions, and health and safety requirements. Have good communication skills. Are willing to undertake training and development as required. The position is part of a small daytime team on campus, working across all university buildings. You will be required to work 20 hours per week, Monday to Friday between 10:00am-2:00pm, although flexibility on the start time will be considered for the successful candidate. The salary shown will be pro-rated down to reflect the part time hours. To view the job description and person specification, please click here Apply now Information at a Glance Share Copy Link Email LinkedIn X Facebook De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance 