    "https://careers.dmu.ac.uk/job/M365-Analyst/553-en_GB": {
      "title": "M365 Analyst Job Details",
      "description": "M365 Analyst Job Details | demontfort M365 Analyst We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs Search Jobs SEARCH VACANCIES HOW TO APPLY RIGHT TO WORK BENEFITS YOUR DEVELOPMENT VISION EDI LOCATIONS FAQs View profile Job Description Job Alerts Link M365 Analyst Apply now Requisition Id: 553 Job Location: Gateway House Full-time/Part-time: Full-time Employee Weekly Hours: 37.00 Maximum Salary: 38,784.00 GBP Minimum Salary: 32,080.00 GBP Market Supplement: Application Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Job Description: Main duties and responsibilities De Montfort University (DMU) is a forward-thinking institution committed to innovation, inclusion and excellent digital services. Following significant progress through its Digital Transformation Strategy, this is an exciting opportunity to contribute to ongoing improvements that support students and staff across a modern, ambitious and evolving university community. Directorate The Digital and Technology Directorate plays a central role in transforming how the university delivers digital value. We are modernising our services through cloud adoption, reducing technical debt and developing a product-focused operating model. Our approach combines agile delivery with operational excellence, ensuring our services are resilient, secure and user focused. From AI and automation to collaboration, communications and cyber security, the Directorate is focused on delivering streamlined and future-ready services that support academic and professional excellence across DMU. The Role We are looking for a motivated and technically capable M365 Analyst to support, improve and develop the university's Microsoft 365 collaboration, communication and digital workplace services. This is a hands-on role that will help shape the digital experience of our students and staff. You will work with senior colleagues and cross-functional teams to support secure, reliable and user-centred Microsoft 365 services, while contributing to DMU’s transformation towards a modern digital workplace. You will support and enhance services across the Microsoft 365 ecosystem, including collaboration and communication tools such as Microsoft Teams, SharePoint Online, OneDrive, Exchange Online and telephony services. The role also involves working with Microsoft Forms, Approvals, Bookings, Viva, Power Automate, the wider Power Platform, Microsoft Entra ID, security, governance and compliance solutions, and emerging AI technologies including Microsoft Copilot. Team Structure You will report to the Productivity and Collaboration Lead and work alongside colleagues supporting Microsoft 365, collaboration, communication and digital workplace services. You will also collaborate with Product teams, Information Security, technical specialists, key suppliers and stakeholders from across the university. The team supports collaboration, communication, automation and AI capabilities across the university and plays a key role in delivering DMU's digital transformation strategy. We promote collaboration, knowledge sharing, continuous improvement and professional development, providing opportunities to build expertise across Microsoft 365, automation, AI and modern workplace technologies. What You'll Be Doing This role supports and enhances Microsoft 365 services across the university, including SharePoint Online and Microsoft Teams Telephony. It involves implementing secure, user-centred solutions, supporting governance and compliance initiatives, contributing to service improvements and digital transformation projects, and working with stakeholders to deliver high-quality digital services while improving adoption, performance and user experience. About You You will have experience supporting and developing Microsoft 365 services within a large organisation, with strong knowledge of technologies including Teams, Exchange Online, SharePoint Online, OneDrive, Viva, Teams Telephony, Entra ID, Power Platform and Microsoft Copilot. You will also bring experience in security, compliance and governance, alongside strong analytical, stakeholder engagement and customer service skills, with a focus on digital transformation and continuous improvement. Contact This role is hybrid, with an on-campus presence required for at least two days per week. To view the JDPS, please click here For any queries regarding this role, please contact Aftab Kharodia - akharodia@dmu.ac.uk Competencies Technical Support Documentation Troubleshooting Collaborative Workload Management Compliance Professional Compliance Skills Problem-Solving Attention to Detail Communication Time Management Flexibility Resilience Collaboration Apply now Information at a Glance Share Copy Link Email LinkedIn X Facebook De Montfort University is committed to providing a working and learning environment that enriches lives, supports individuals to reach their full potential, and where everyone is treated with dignity and respect. As an educator and shaper of society, the university aims to role model positive behaviours both within the university and to reflect the diversity of the wider community. As such we welcome applications from all potential candidates. For general enquiries, please contact peopleservices@dmu.ac.uk Accessibility Legal Modern Slavery Act statements Privacy Cookie Consent Manager Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2025 De Montfort University × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and